.policy "python-practice-cancellation-swallowed" revision 1
.description "Re-raise asyncio.CancelledError wherever an async def catches or suppresses it; swallowing it breaks cancel(), timeouts and task groups."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. asyncio implements Task.cancel(), asyncio.timeout(), wait_for() and TaskGroup by
// throwing CancelledError into the coroutine. A coroutine that catches it and goes on keeps running after it was
// cancelled, and the coroutine that awaits it resumes as if the work had finished: a timeout no longer fires, a
// TaskGroup waits for it, shutdown hangs.
// It reports, in an `async def`'s own frame (a nested sync def or lambda is its own frame) and outside test code:
//   - an `except` clause that catches cancellation, `asyncio.CancelledError` (also through `asyncio.exceptions`, an
//     alias or a tuple), `BaseException`, or a bare `except:`, of a try whose body awaits (`await`, `async with`,
//     `async for`) in the same frame, when some path through the handler ends without re-raising: it falls through,
//     returns, breaks, continues, or raises another exception first;
//   - a `with contextlib.suppress(...)` naming one of those classes whose body awaits, when more of the function runs
//     after it (a later statement, or the next turn of a loop around it).
//   async def poll(c):
//       try: await c.get()
//       except asyncio.CancelledError: log.info("stopped")          reported: falls through
//       except asyncio.CancelledError: break                         reported
//       except asyncio.CancelledError: raise ConnectionError()       reported: another exception
//       except asyncio.CancelledError: await c.close(); raise        not reported
//       with contextlib.suppress(asyncio.CancelledError): await c.get()
//       log.info("go on")                                            the `with` is reported
// A handler re-raises on a path when it ends in a bare `raise`, `raise <the caught name>`, `raise CancelledError()`,
// a raise of a BaseExceptionGroup (or a subclass, through imports and aliases; the `exceptiongroup` backport too)
// whose arguments carry the caught name, directly, in a list or tuple, or through a name the handler binds to them
// (`errors = [exc, other]`, `errors.append(exc)`), an `if` whose every branch (with an `else`) re-raises or tests
// `isinstance(e, T)` with T a class a cancellation is not (`if isinstance(e, OSError): ... else: raise`), a `with`
// whose body does, a nested `try` whose `finally` does, `if isinstance(e, CancelledError): raise` (the handler also
// catches Exception), or a call of a function of the run whose body always raises (a helper that surfaces the
// exception it is given); and no statement before that returns, breaks, continues or raises something else.
// `raise ExceptionGroup("...", [exc])` is no re-raise: an ExceptionGroup refuses a BaseException such as
// CancelledError and raises TypeError instead.
// It leaves alone the idioms a reviewer accepts:
//   - the drain: `t.cancel()` (or `for t in ts: t.cancel()`) earlier in the same function, or in a helper of the same
//     class (or a base) or module that the call graph resolves (`self._stop()`, whose body, or a helper it calls,
//     cancels `self._task`), and the try body (or the suppress body) awaits `t`, `asyncio.gather(*ts)`,
//     `asyncio.wait_for(t, ...)` or `asyncio.shield(t)`: the CancelledError is the child's. t is compared by its
//     text: a dotted name (`self._task`) or a subscript (`self.tasks[k]`). `asyncio.wait(ts)` is not a drain: it
//     never raises a child's CancelledError, so the one caught there is the function's own;
//   - a handler that reads `asyncio.current_task().cancelling()` (or calls `uncancel()`) and has a `raise`;
//   - the coroutine an event-loop runner starts, also at module level: `asyncio.run(main())`, `uvloop.run(main())`,
//     `loop.run_until_complete(main())`, `asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe(main(), loop)`, `.run(main())` on an
//     `asyncio.Runner(...)` (built in the call, or bound in the same frame by `with asyncio.Runner() as r` or
//     `r = asyncio.Runner()`), and the function `anyio.run(main)` / `trio.run(main)` take (also inside
//     `functools.partial(main, ...)`): cancelling it is the shutdown. The runners are a list of library entry
//     points resolved through imports; nothing in the code says that a call starts a loop otherwise;
//   - a handler that ends its function, when no code of the run resumes after it: the try is a statement of the body
//     (or of a `with`/`async with` that is), or of a top-level loop the handler leaves with `break`/`return`, and
//     nothing follows but a `return` without a value (or `return None`), and the handler returns no value either:
//     the function hands its awaiter no partial result as a success, and an async generator yields nothing more;
//     and either the function only ever runs as a task
//     (`asyncio.create_task(pump())`, `loop.create_task(...)`, `ensure_future`, or a helper of the run that spawns
//     its first argument, `safe_create_task(pump())`), or no code of the run awaits it: every call of it is handed
//     to a call that is not awaited, not an asyncio function and not a def of the run that awaits a parameter
//     (`StreamingResponse(events(q))`), it is passed uncalled (`scheduler.add_job(self.refresh)`), or it is
//     registered by a decorator called on an object (`@router.websocket("/ws")`), and the handler only records or
//     logs (no await, yield or raise). An async generator that yields after the handler, or whose handler yields, is
//     not this case:
//       async def events(q):                 return StreamingResponse(events(q))
//           try: async for e in q: yield e
//           except asyncio.CancelledError: log.info("client went away")     not reported
//       async def download(c):               ... await download(c) elsewhere in the run
//           while True:
//               try: pages.append(await c.next())
//               except asyncio.CancelledError: break                        reported: the caller resumes
//           return pages
//   - a deferred re-raise: the handler sets a flag (`cancelled = True`), and a later `if cancelled: raise
//     asyncio.CancelledError` in the same function raises it after the bookkeeping;
//   - a handler or suppress inside a cancellation handler that re-raises on every path (`except CancelledError: try:
//     await shield(close()) except CancelledError: pass; raise`): the outer `raise` carries the cancellation on;
//   - anyio and trio code: a handler that catches cancellation only as `BaseException` or a bare `except:` (or a
//     `suppress(BaseException)`), in a function whose own frame uses anyio or trio (a name that resolves into
//     `anyio` or `trio`: `anyio.CancelScope`, `move_on_after`, a task group). anyio and trio cancel scopes are
//     level-triggered: a swallowed cancellation is delivered again at the next checkpoint, so nothing hangs. An
//     explicit `except asyncio.CancelledError` there is still reported;
//   - `except Exception` (CancelledError is a BaseException since Python 3.8), a sync def, a try body that does not
//     await (`fut.result()` raises the future's own cancellation), an application class named CancelledError, and
//     `concurrent.futures.CancelledError`;
//   - test files.
// Gaps: a drain whose task travels through another name (`t = self._task; self._task.cancel(); await t`) is
// reported, and so is a cancel in a helper the call graph cannot resolve; a handler that sets a flag a loop reads
// and then exits cleanly is reported; a CancelledError that an async generator or a library hands up from a child it
// cancelled (not this function's own) is reported when the function does not cancel it by name; a function that only
// code outside the run awaits (a library's public coroutine handed to nothing) is reported, while one handed to an
// outside API that awaits it and resumes (`await lib.retry(self.fetch)` is awaited and counts; a bare
// `lib.schedule(fetch())` does not) is taken as ended; a suppress that ends its function is left alone; an exception
// group class bound by an assignment (`Group = BaseExceptionGroup`) is not resolved; anyio is decided per function,
// so a function that uses no anyio name but runs inside an anyio scope is read as asyncio code; a handler inside an
// anyio shielded scope that names asyncio.CancelledError is reported.

#include "lib/python_practice.rerail"
#include "python/exceptions.rerail"
#include "python/flow.rerail"

// What crosses files is over symbols (decision 0677: no node crosses files): a def by its symbol, a call, a handler or
// a guard by its term. A helper that always raises, a helper that cancels, a runner, a spawner and the callers of a
// function may be in other files: each file states its own by symbol and term, and the finding reads the answers by
// its handler's, its guard's and its function's.
.violation CancellationSwallowed(at: node)
    "Re-raise the CancelledError at the end of this handler (`raise` after cleanup); swallowing it breaks cancel(), asyncio.timeout() and TaskGroup. Leave it if this function cancelled the task it awaits."
CancellationSwallowed(x) :- pcs_handler(x, t, f), pcs_awaits(t, f), !pcs_drain_here(t, f), !pcs_checks_cancelling(x),
    !pcs_deferred(x, f), !pcs_anyio_handler(x, f), pp_live(x), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(t, tt), pt_def(f, fq),
    !pcs_reraised(xt), !pcs_drain_at(tt), !pcs_runner_entry(fq), !pcs_task_end(xt), !pcs_inside_ok(xt).

.violation CancellationSuppressed(at: node)
    "Use try/except with a final `raise` instead of suppress() for CancelledError: the code after this block runs on after a cancel. Leave it if this function cancelled the task it awaits."
CancellationSuppressed(w) :- pcs_suppress(w, f), pcs_awaits(w, f), !pcs_drain_here(w, f), !pcs_end_pos(w, f),
    !pcs_anyio_suppress(w, f), pp_live(w), pt_tm(w, wt), pt_def(f, fq), !pcs_drain_at(wt), !pcs_runner_entry(fq),
    !pcs_inside_ok(wt).

// pcs_handler(x, t, f): except clause x of try t, in async def f's own frame, catches cancellation.
.decl pcs_handler(x: node, t: node, f: node)
pcs_handler(x, t, f) :- exc_handler(t, x), pcs_catches(x), pp_frame(x, f), pp_async_def(f).
.decl pcs_catches(x: node)
pcs_catches(x) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), !field(x, "value", _).
pcs_catches(x) :- exc_type(x, e), exc_qual(e, q), pcs_cancel_q(q).
pcs_catches(x) :- exc_type(x, e), exc_qual(e, "builtins.BaseException").
.decl pcs_cancel_q(q: symbol)
pcs_cancel_q("asyncio.CancelledError"). pcs_cancel_q("asyncio.exceptions.CancelledError").
// pcs_names_asyncio(x): handler x names asyncio's CancelledError itself, not only BaseException or nothing.
.decl pcs_names_asyncio(x: node)
pcs_names_asyncio(x) :- exc_type(x, e), exc_qual(e, q), pcs_cancel_q(q).

// pcs_suppress(w, f): `with contextlib.suppress(...)` w, in async def f's own frame, suppresses cancellation.
.decl pcs_suppress(w: node, f: node)
pcs_suppress(w, f) :- pcs_suppress_arg(w, a), (pcs_names_cancel(a) ; exc_qual(a, "builtins.BaseException")),
    pp_frame(w, f), pp_async_def(f).
// pcs_suppress_arg(w, a): a is an argument of a `contextlib.suppress(...)` item of with statement w.
.decl pcs_suppress_arg(w: node, a: node)
pcs_suppress_arg(w, a) :- kind(w, "with_statement"), child(w, wc, _), kind(wc, "with_clause"), child(wc, it, _),
    kind(it, "with_item"), field(it, "value", v0), (kind(v0, "as_pattern"), child(v0, v1, 0) ;
    !kind(v0, "as_pattern"), v1 = v0), unparen(v1, c), exc_call(c, "contextlib.suppress"), exc_arg(c, _, a).
.decl pcs_suppress_names_asyncio(w: node)
pcs_suppress_names_asyncio(w) :- pcs_suppress_arg(w, a), pcs_names_cancel(a).

// pcs_guard(t, f): try t of a cancellation handler, or suppress-with t, in async def f.
.decl pcs_guard(t: node, f: node)
pcs_guard(t, f) :- pcs_handler(_, t, f).
pcs_guard(w, f) :- pcs_suppress(w, f).
// pcs_awaits(t, f): guard t's body suspends in f's own frame: an await, `async with` or `async for`.
.decl pcs_awaits(t: node, f: node)
pcs_awaits(t, f) :- pcs_guard(t, f), field(t, "body", tb), pcs_suspend(w), within(w, tb), pp_frame(w, f).
.decl pcs_suspend(w: node)
pcs_suspend(w) :- kind(w, "await").
pcs_suspend(w) :- (kind(w, "with_statement") ; kind(w, "for_statement") ; kind(w, "for_in_clause")), op(w, "async").

// ---- re-raise paths ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A handler re-raises when every path through its body does: some statement of a block always re-raises, and no
// statement before it may leave the block another way. A call statement re-raises when a helper it surely calls
// always raises, which is known only across files; so each file states its handlers' bodies as and/or trees over
// their blocks, statements and clauses, by their terms (pcs_t_or, pcs_t_and, pcs_t_leaf, pcs_t_call: x the handler's
// term, n a node's, true when ...), and the tree is read with the helpers' answers (pcs_t, pcs_reraised).
// pcs_block_of(x, b): b is handler x's body or a block inside it, in the same frame.
.decl pcs_block_of(x: node, b: node)
pcs_block_of(x, b) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), exc_body(x, b).
pcs_block_of(x, b) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), exc_body(x, hb), kind(b, "block"), within(b, hb), pp_frame(b, f).
// pcs_stmt(x, s): s is a statement of a block of handler x.
.decl pcs_stmt(x: node, s: node)
pcs_stmt(x, s) :- pcs_block_of(x, b), child(b, s, _).
// n is true when m is: a block when one of its statements is that no statement before may leave by; a `with` when
// its body is; a `try` when its `finally` is; `if isinstance(e, CancelledError):` when its branch is (the path the
// cancellation takes); an if or elif clause whose condition tests the caught exception against classes a cancellation
// is not, when the clauses after it are (pcs_other_test); an else clause when its body is.
.decl pcs_t_or(xt: symbol, n: symbol, m: symbol)
pcs_t_or(xt, bt, st) :- pcs_block_of(x, b), child(b, s, j), !kind(s, "comment"), !pcs_exit_before(x, b, j),
    pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(b, bt), pt_tm(s, st).
pcs_t_or(xt, st, mt) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), kind(s, "with_statement"), field(s, "body", m), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st),
    pt_tm(m, mt).
pcs_t_or(xt, st, mt) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), kind(s, "try_statement"), child(s, fc, _), kind(fc, "finally_clause"),
    child(fc, m, _), kind(m, "block"), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st), pt_tm(m, mt).
pcs_t_or(xt, st, mt) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "condition", kc), pcs_is_cancel_test(x, kc),
    field(s, "consequence", m), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st), pt_tm(m, mt).
pcs_t_or(xt, st, yt) :- pcs_clause(x, s, kc, _, y), pcs_other_test(x, kc), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st), pt_tm(y, yt).
pcs_t_or(xt, yt, mt) :- pcs_clause(x, _, _, _, y), pcs_else(x, y, m), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(y, yt), pt_tm(m, mt).
// n is true when both m1 and m2 are: an if or elif clause when its branch is and the clauses after it are.
.decl pcs_t_and(xt: symbol, n: symbol, m1: symbol, m2: symbol)
pcs_t_and(xt, st, ct, yt) :- pcs_clause(x, s, _, c, y), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st), pt_tm(c, ct), pt_tm(y, yt).
// pcs_clause(x, s, kc, c, y): if statement or elif clause s, in handler x, tests kc, runs c, and has clause y next.
// pcs_else(x, y, b): else clause y, after such a clause, runs b.
.decl pcs_clause(x: node, s: node, kc: node, c: node, y: node)
pcs_clause(x, s, kc, c, y) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "condition", kc),
    field(s, "consequence", c), alt_first(s, y).
pcs_clause(x, y, kc, c, z) :- pcs_clause(x, _, _, _, y), kind(y, "elif_clause"), field(y, "condition", kc),
    field(y, "consequence", c), alt_next(y, z).
.decl pcs_else(x: node, y: node, b: node)
pcs_else(x, y, b) :- pcs_clause(x, _, _, _, y), kind(y, "else_clause"), field(y, "body", b).
// n is true: a re-raise (pcs_reraise_stmt).
.decl pcs_t_leaf(xt: symbol, n: symbol)
pcs_t_leaf(xt, st) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), pcs_reraise_stmt(x, s), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st).
// n is true when the call whose term is c raises: a call statement with a sure target (`_surface(exc)`).
.decl pcs_t_call(xt: symbol, n: symbol, ct: symbol)
pcs_t_call(xt, st, ct) :- pcs_stmt(x, s), kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, e, 0), unparen(e, c),
    pp_sure_target(c, _), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(s, st), pt_tm(c, ct).
// pcs_t(x, n): node n of handler x's tree is true. pcs_reraised(x): handler x's body is.
.decl pcs_t(xt: symbol, n: symbol)
pcs_t(xt, n) :- pcs_t_leaf(xt, n).
pcs_t(xt, n) :- pcs_t_call(xt, n, ct), pcs_raising(ct).
pcs_t(xt, n) :- pcs_t_or(xt, n, m), pcs_t(xt, m).
pcs_t(xt, n) :- pcs_t_and(xt, n, m1, m2), pcs_t(xt, m1), pcs_t(xt, m2).
.decl pcs_reraised(xt: symbol)
pcs_reraised(xt) :- pcs_body_at(xt, bt), pcs_t(xt, bt).
.decl pcs_body_at(xt: symbol, bt: symbol)
pcs_body_at(xt, bt) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), exc_body(x, b), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_tm(b, bt).
// pcs_raising(c): a sure target of the call whose term is c is a def of the run whose body always raises (a helper
// that surfaces the exception it is given). pcs_raises_def(g): stated in g's file.
.decl pcs_raising(ct: symbol)
pcs_raising(ct) :- pp_sure_at(ct, g), pcs_raises_def(g).
.decl pcs_raises_def(g: symbol)
pcs_raises_def(gq) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), field(g, "body", gb), always_raises(gb), pt_def(g, gq).
// pcs_reraise_stmt(x, r): a bare `raise`, `raise <the name x binds>`, a raise of a new CancelledError, or a raise of
// an exception group that carries the caught exception.
.decl pcs_reraise_stmt(x: node, r: node)
pcs_reraise_stmt(x, r) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), kind(r, "raise_statement"), !exc_raise(r, _), within(r, x).
pcs_reraise_stmt(x, r) :- exc_alias(x, a), exc_raise(r, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, a), within(r, x).
pcs_reraise_stmt(x, r) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), exc_raise(r, e), exc_class(e, c), exc_qual(c, q), pcs_cancel_q(q),
    within(r, x).
pcs_reraise_stmt(x, r) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), exc_raise(r, e), within(r, x), pcs_group_call(e),
    pcs_call_value(e, v), pcs_carries(x, v).
// pcs_group_call(e): raised call e builds a BaseExceptionGroup (builtin or the exceptiongroup backport) or a class of
// the run built on one (its ancestry read through python/names' phase, by the module the class's name reads).
// ExceptionGroup is left out: it refuses a BaseException and raises TypeError.
.decl pcs_group_call(e: node)
pcs_group_call(e) :- exc_raise(_, e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), exc_qual(fn, q),
    (q = "builtins.BaseExceptionGroup" ; q = "exceptiongroup.BaseExceptionGroup").
pcs_group_call(e) :- exc_raise(_, e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), exc_qual(fn, q), docof(e, d),
    doc(d, p, _), py_names__reads_at(p, m), py_names__ancestor(m, q, b),
    (b = "builtins.BaseExceptionGroup" ; b = "exceptiongroup.BaseExceptionGroup").
// pcs_call_value(e, v): v is a positional or keyword argument of call e, parentheses off.
.decl pcs_call_value(e: node, v: node)
pcs_call_value(e, v) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "arguments", l), kind(l, "argument_list"), child(l, a0, _),
    !kind(a0, "comment"), (kind(a0, "keyword_argument"), field(a0, "value", a1) ;
    !kind(a0, "keyword_argument"), a1 = a0), unparen(a1, v).
// pcs_carries(x, v): expression v, in handler x, holds the exception x caught: its name, a name x binds to a value
// that holds it, or a list or tuple with such an element.
.decl pcs_carries(x: node, v: node)
pcs_carries(x, v) :- exc_alias(x, a), kind(v, "identifier"), within(v, x), text(v, a).
pcs_carries(x, v) :- pcs_carrier(x, c), kind(v, "identifier"), within(v, x), text(v, c).
pcs_carries(x, v) :- (kind(v, "list") ; kind(v, "tuple")), within(v, x), child(v, e0, _), unparen(e0, e),
    pcs_carries(x, e).
// pcs_carrier(x, c): handler x binds name c to a value holding the caught exception (`c = [exc, other]`), or
// appends one to it (`c.append(exc)`).
.decl pcs_carrier(x: node, c: symbol)
pcs_carrier(x, c) :- exc_alias(x, _), kind(a, "assignment"), within(a, x), field(a, "left", l),
    kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, c), field(a, "right", r0), unparen(r0, r), pcs_carries(x, r).
pcs_carrier(x, c) :- exc_alias(x, _), kind(k, "call"), within(k, x), field(k, "function", fn),
    attr_of(fn, o, "append"), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, c), exc_arg(k, 0, v), pcs_carries(x, v).
// pcs_is_cancel_test(x, k): k is `isinstance(<the name x binds>, T)` with T CancelledError or a tuple holding it.
.decl pcs_is_cancel_test(x: node, k: node)
pcs_is_cancel_test(x, k) :- exc_alias(x, a), unparen(k, c), exc_call(c, "builtins.isinstance"), exc_arg(c, 0, v),
    kind(v, "identifier"), text(v, a), exc_arg(c, 1, t), pcs_names_cancel(t).
.decl pcs_names_cancel(t: node)
pcs_names_cancel(t) :- exc_qual(t, q), pcs_cancel_q(q).
pcs_names_cancel(t) :- kind(t, "tuple"), child(t, e0, _), unparen(e0, e), exc_qual(e, q), pcs_cancel_q(q).
// pcs_other_test(x, k): k is `isinstance(<the name x binds>, T)` with T neither CancelledError nor BaseException, nor
// a tuple holding one: a cancellation does not take that branch.
.decl pcs_other_test(x: node, k: node)
pcs_other_test(x, k) :- exc_alias(x, a), unparen(k, c), exc_call(c, "builtins.isinstance"), exc_arg(c, 0, v),
    kind(v, "identifier"), text(v, a), exc_arg(c, 1, t), !pcs_names_cancel(t), !pcs_names_base(t).
.decl pcs_names_base(t: node)
pcs_names_base(t) :- exc_qual(t, "builtins.BaseException").
pcs_names_base(t) :- kind(t, "tuple"), child(t, e0, _), unparen(e0, e), exc_qual(e, "builtins.BaseException").
// pcs_exit_before(x, b, j): a statement of b before position j may leave b without re-raising: it holds a return,
// a raise of something else, or a break/continue that is not inside a loop of its own.
.decl pcs_exit_before(x: node, b: node, j: number)
pcs_exit_before(x, b, j) :- pcs_block_of(x, b), child(b, s, i), i < j, child(b, _, j), pcs_exit_in(x, s).
.decl pcs_exit_in(x: node, s: node)
pcs_exit_in(x, s) :- pcs_block_of(x, b), child(b, s, _), pcs_handler(x, _, f), pcs_exit(x, e),
    (e = s ; within(e, s)), pp_frame(e, f), !pcs_loop_between(e, s).
.decl pcs_exit(x: node, e: node)
pcs_exit(x, e) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), within(e, x), kind(e, "return_statement").
pcs_exit(x, e) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), within(e, x), (kind(e, "break_statement") ; kind(e, "continue_statement")).
pcs_exit(x, e) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), within(e, x), kind(e, "raise_statement"), !pcs_reraise_stmt(x, e).
// pcs_loop_between(e, s): a break or continue e targets a loop inside statement s (or s itself is that loop).
.decl pcs_loop_between(e: node, s: node)
pcs_loop_between(e, s) :- (kind(e, "break_statement") ; kind(e, "continue_statement")),
    (kind(l, "for_statement") ; kind(l, "while_statement")), within(e, l), (l = s ; within(l, s)).

// ---- drains ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A drain: guard t's body awaits a task or future that f cancelled before: `D` itself, or `D`/`*D` handed to
// asyncio.gather, wait_for or shield, where `D.cancel()` (or `v.cancel()` in a loop or comprehension over D) comes
// earlier in f's own frame (pcs_drain_here), or in a helper f calls earlier (pcs_drain_at). D is compared by its text:
// `task`, `self._task`, `self.tasks[k]`.
.decl pcs_drain_here(t: node, f: node)
pcs_drain_here(t, f) :- pcs_drain_wait(t, f, w, d), pcs_cancelled(f, d, cc), earlier(cc, w).
// pcs_drain_wait(t, f, w, d): guard t's body awaits D (by its text d) at w, in f's own frame.
.decl pcs_drain_wait(t: node, f: node, w: node, d: symbol)
pcs_drain_wait(t, f, w, d) :- pcs_awaits(t, f), field(t, "body", tb), kind(w, "await"), within(w, tb), pp_frame(w, f),
    child(w, e0, 0), unparen(e0, e), pcs_drained(e, d).
// pcs_key(e, d): e's text as a drain compares it: a dotted name, or a subscript as written.
.decl pcs_key(e: node, d: symbol)
pcs_key(e, d) :- dotted_expr(e, d).
pcs_key(e, d) :- kind(e, "subscript"), text(e, d).
// pcs_drained(e, d): the awaited expression e waits for D, by D's text d.
.decl pcs_drained(e: node, d: symbol)
pcs_drained(e, d) :- pcs_key(e, d).
pcs_drained(e, d) :- exc_call(e, q), (q = "asyncio.gather" ; q = "asyncio.wait_for" ; q = "asyncio.shield"),
    field(e, "arguments", l), child(l, a0, _), (kind(a0, "list_splat"), child(a0, a, 0) ; !kind(a0, "list_splat"),
    a = a0), pcs_key(a, d).
// pcs_cancelled(f, d, cc): call cc, in f's own frame, cancels D or each item of D.
.decl pcs_cancelled(f: node, d: symbol, cc: node)
pcs_cancelled(f, d, cc) :- pcs_cancel_call(cc, r), pcs_key(r, d), pp_frame(cc, f).
pcs_cancelled(f, d, cc) :- pcs_cancel_call(cc, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, v),
    (kind(l, "for_statement") ; kind(l, "for_in_clause")), field(l, "left", lv), text(lv, v), field(l, "right", it),
    pcs_key(it, d), pcs_loop_holds(l, cc), pp_frame(cc, f).
.decl pcs_cancel_call(cc: node, r: node)
pcs_cancel_call(cc, r) :- kind(cc, "call"), field(cc, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, r, "cancel").
// pcs_loop_holds(l, cc): cc runs once per item of loop l: in a for statement's body, or in the body of l's
// comprehension.
.decl pcs_loop_holds(l: node, cc: node)
pcs_loop_holds(l, cc) :- kind(l, "for_statement"), field(l, "body", b), within(cc, b).
pcs_loop_holds(l, cc) :- kind(l, "for_in_clause"), child(m, l, _), field(m, "body", b), (cc = b ; within(cc, b)).
// Helpers, over symbols. pcs_drain_via(t, h, g, d): before guard t (by its term) awaits D, a call in its function f's
// own frame surely calls g, where f's home is h. pcs_drain_at(t): such a g is a helper f may use (pcs_home_ok) and
// cancels D (pcs_cancels).
.decl pcs_drain_via(tt: symbol, h: symbol, g: symbol, d: symbol)
pcs_drain_via(tt, h, g, d) :- pcs_drain_wait(t, f, w, d), kind(s, "call"), pp_sure_target(s, g), pp_frame(s, f),
    earlier(s, w), pcs_home_of(f, h), pt_tm(t, tt).
.decl pcs_drain_at(tt: symbol)
pcs_drain_at(tt) :- pcs_drain_via(tt, h, g, d), pcs_home(g, hg), pcs_home_ok(h, hg), pcs_cancels(g, d).
// pcs_cancels(g, d): def g's own frame cancels D, or calls a helper that does. pcs_helper(f, h, g): a call in def f's
// own frame (f's home h) surely calls g. Stated in f's file.
.decl pcs_cancels(g: symbol, d: symbol)
pcs_cancels(gq, d) :- pcs_cancelled(g, d, _), pt_def(g, gq).
pcs_cancels(fq, d) :- pcs_helper(fq, h, g), pcs_home(g, hg), pcs_home_ok(h, hg), pcs_cancels(g, d).
.decl pcs_helper(f: symbol, h: symbol, g: symbol)
pcs_helper(fq, h, g) :- kind(s, "call"), pp_sure_target(s, g), pp_frame(s, f), pcs_home_of(f, h), pt_def(f, fq).
// pcs_home_of(f, h): def f's home: the class it is a method of (h its symbol), or, for a module-level def, its module
// (h "file:" and its path). pcs_home(g, h): by g's symbol. A helper of f is a def of f's home or, for a method, of a
// base class of it (pcs_home_ok): there `self.x` and a global name mean the same.
.decl pcs_home_of(f: node, h: symbol)
pcs_home_of(f, cq) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), pp_frame(f, c), kind(c, "class_definition"), class_def(c, cq).
pcs_home_of(f, cat("file:", p)) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), !pp_frame(f, _), docof(f, d), doc(d, p, _).
.decl pcs_home(g: symbol, h: symbol)
pcs_home(gq, h) :- pcs_home_of(g, h), pt_def(g, gq).
.decl pcs_home_ok(h: symbol, hg: symbol)
pcs_home_ok(h, h) :- pcs_home(_, h).
pcs_home_ok(h, hg) :- pcs_home(_, h), subclass(h, hg), pcs_home(_, hg).

// pcs_checks_cancelling(x): handler x asks the current task whether it is being cancelled, and has a raise.
.decl pcs_checks_cancelling(x: node)
pcs_checks_cancelling(x) :- exc_body(x, b), kind(c, "call"), within(c, b), field(c, "function", fn),
    (attr_of(fn, _, "cancelling") ; attr_of(fn, _, "uncancel")), kind(r, "raise_statement"), within(r, b).

// ---- runners -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// pcs_runner_entry(f): f is the coroutine an event-loop runner starts, also at module level: handed as a coroutine
// (`asyncio.run(f())`) or, to anyio and trio, as the function (`anyio.run(f)`). By f's symbol: the runner may be in
// another file.
.decl pcs_runner_entry(f: symbol)
pcs_runner_entry(fq) :- pcs_coro_runner(c), exc_arg(c, 0, a), kind(a, "call"), call_target(a, fq).
pcs_runner_entry(fq) :- pcs_runner_ref(k, x), pcs_ref_def(k, x, fq).
.decl pcs_runner_ref(k: symbol, x: symbol)
pcs_runner_ref(k, x) :- exc_call(c, q), (q = "anyio.run" ; q = "trio.run"), exc_arg(c, 0, a), pcs_ref(a, k, x).
// pcs_coro_runner(c): call c runs the coroutine it is given on an event loop and returns its result.
.decl pcs_coro_runner(c: node)
pcs_coro_runner(c) :- exc_call(c, q), (q = "asyncio.run" ; q = "uvloop.run" ; q = "asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe").
pcs_coro_runner(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, _, "run_until_complete").
pcs_coro_runner(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "run"), pcs_runner_obj(o).
// pcs_runner_obj(o): o is an asyncio.Runner: built in place, or a name bound to one in the same frame.
.decl pcs_runner_obj(o: node)
pcs_runner_obj(o) :- attr_of(_, o, "run"), unparen(o, m), exc_call(m, "asyncio.Runner").
pcs_runner_obj(o) :- attr_of(_, o, "run"), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, v), pcs_runner_bind(b, v),
    pp_frame(o, h), pp_frame(b, h).
pcs_runner_obj(o) :- attr_of(_, o, "run"), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, v), !pp_frame(o, _), docof(o, d),
    pcs_runner_bind(b, v), !pp_frame(b, _), docof(b, d).
// pcs_runner_bind(b, v): `with asyncio.Runner() as v` (b the as-pattern) or `v = asyncio.Runner()` (b the
// assignment).
.decl pcs_runner_bind(b: node, v: symbol)
pcs_runner_bind(b, v) :- kind(b, "as_pattern"), child(b, m0, 0), unparen(m0, m), exc_call(m, "asyncio.Runner"),
    field(b, "alias", t), child(t, n, 0), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, v).
pcs_runner_bind(b, v) :- kind(b, "assignment"), field(b, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v),
    field(b, "right", r0), unparen(r0, r), exc_call(r, "asyncio.Runner").

// ---- the handler ends the function -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Over symbols: the function f a handler ends (by its symbol), its calls anywhere in the run (by their terms).
// pcs_task_end(x): the handler whose term is x ends its function f, and no code of the run resumes after f: f only
// ever runs as a task's top coroutine, or no code of the run awaits f and the handler only records or logs.
.decl pcs_task_end(xt: symbol)
pcs_task_end(xt) :- pcs_end_at(xt, f, "spawned"), pcs_spawned(f), !pcs_called_otherwise(f).
pcs_task_end(xt) :- pcs_end_at(xt, f, "handed"), pcs_handed_off(f), !pcs_consumed(f).
// pcs_end_at(x, f, how): handler x ends f and returns no value (how "spawned"), and also only records or logs (how
// "handed"). Stated in their file.
.decl pcs_end_at(xt: symbol, f: symbol, how: symbol)
pcs_end_at(xt, fq, "spawned") :- pcs_ends(x, f), !pcs_handler_returns(x), pt_tm(x, xt), pt_def(f, fq).
pcs_end_at(xt, fq, "handed") :- pcs_ends(x, f), !pcs_handler_returns(x), !pcs_handler_acts(x), pt_tm(x, xt),
    pt_def(f, fq).
// pcs_ends(x, f): handler x's try is a statement of a tail block of f, or of the body of a loop that is, when x then
// ends in `break` or `return`; and only a `return` without a value follows.
.decl pcs_ends(x: node, f: node)
pcs_ends(x, f) :- pcs_handler(x, t, f), pcs_end_pos(t, f).
pcs_ends(x, f) :- pcs_handler(x, t, f), pcs_end_pos(l, f), (kind(l, "while_statement") ; kind(l, "for_statement")),
    field(l, "body", lb), child(lb, t, _), pcs_leaves(x).
// pcs_end_pos(n, f): statement n of a tail block of f is followed by nothing but returns without a value.
.decl pcs_end_pos(n: node, f: node)
pcs_end_pos(n, f) :- pcs_tail_block(f, b), child(b, n, i), !kind(n, "comment"), !pcs_runs_after(b, i).
// pcs_tail_block(f, b): b is async def f's body, or the body of a `with`/`async with` at an end position of one.
.decl pcs_tail_block(f: node, b: node)
pcs_tail_block(f, b) :- pp_async_def(f), field(f, "body", b).
pcs_tail_block(f, wb) :- pcs_tail_block(f, b), child(b, s, k), kind(s, "with_statement"), !pcs_runs_after(b, k),
    field(s, "body", wb).
// pcs_runs_after(b, i): a statement of block b after position i does more than `return` or `return None`.
.decl pcs_seq(b: node)
pcs_seq(b) :- pp_async_def(f), field(f, "body", b).
pcs_seq(b) :- kind(s, "with_statement"), field(s, "body", b), pp_frame(s, f), pp_async_def(f).
.decl pcs_last_live(b: node, j: number)
pcs_last_live(b, j) :- pcs_seq(b), j = max k : { child(b, s, k), !kind(s, "comment"), !pcs_empty_return(s) }.
.decl pcs_runs_after(b: node, i: number)
pcs_runs_after(b, i) :- pcs_last_live(b, j), child(b, _, i), i < j.
// pcs_empty_return(s): `return` or `return None`.
.decl pcs_empty_return(s: node)
pcs_empty_return(s) :- kind(s, "return_statement"), !pcs_return_value(s, _).
pcs_empty_return(s) :- kind(s, "return_statement"), pcs_return_value(s, v), kind(v, "none").
.decl pcs_return_value(s: node, v: node)
pcs_return_value(s, v) :- kind(s, "return_statement"), child(s, v0, _), !kind(v0, "comment"), unparen(v0, v).
// pcs_handler_returns(x): handler x returns a value other than None in its function's frame.
.decl pcs_handler_returns(x: node)
pcs_handler_returns(x) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), exc_body(x, b), kind(s, "return_statement"), within(s, b),
    pp_frame(s, f), !pcs_empty_return(s).
// pcs_leaves(x): the last statement of handler x's body is a `break` or a `return`.
.decl pcs_leaves(x: node)
pcs_leaves(x) :- pcs_handler(x, _, _), exc_body(x, b), j = max k : { child(b, s2, k), !kind(s2, "comment") },
    child(b, s, j), (kind(s, "break_statement") ; kind(s, "return_statement")).
// pcs_handler_acts(x): handler x does more than record or log: it awaits, yields or raises in its function's frame.
.decl pcs_handler_acts(x: node)
pcs_handler_acts(x) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), exc_body(x, b), within(n, b), pp_frame(n, f),
    (pcs_suspend(n) ; kind(n, "yield") ; kind(n, "raise_statement")).

// Tasks. pcs_spawn_arg(c): the call whose term is c is the coroutine handed to a spawn call, or to a helper of the
// run that spawns its first parameter (`def safe_create_task(coro): ... asyncio.create_task(wrapper())` with `await
// coro` in wrapper). The helper is the def the callee names through imports (pcs_spawn_via, by its qualified name),
// not the call program's target: a tracing decorator on the helper (letta's `@trace_method`) makes the call program
// answer with the decorator's wrapper.
.decl pcs_spawn_arg(ct: symbol)
pcs_spawn_arg(ct) :- pcs_spawn_direct(ct).
pcs_spawn_arg(ct) :- pcs_spawn_via(ct, q), pcs_spawner_q(q).
.decl pcs_spawn_direct(ct: symbol)
pcs_spawn_direct(ct) :- pp_spawn_call(sc, _), exc_arg(sc, 0, c), kind(c, "call"), pt_tm(c, ct).
.decl pcs_spawn_via(ct: symbol, q: symbol)
pcs_spawn_via(ct, q) :- kind(sc, "call"), field(sc, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), exc_arg(sc, 0, c), kind(c, "call"),
    pt_tm(c, ct).
.decl pcs_spawner_q(q: symbol)
pcs_spawner_q(q) :- pcs_spawner(g), qualname(g, q).
.decl pcs_spawner(g: node)
pcs_spawner(g) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), sig_param(g, _, nm, 0, _, _, _), text(nm, p), p != "self",
    pp_spawn_call(sc, _), within(sc, g), pcs_param_spawned(g, sc, p).
.decl pcs_param_spawned(g: node, sc: node, p: symbol)
pcs_param_spawned(g, sc, p) :- pp_spawn_call(sc, _), within(sc, g), exc_arg(sc, 0, a), kind(a, "identifier"),
    text(a, p).
pcs_param_spawned(g, sc, p) :- pp_spawn_call(sc, _), within(sc, g), kind(w, "await"), within(w, g), child(w, e0, 0),
    unparen(e0, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, p).
.decl pcs_spawned(f: symbol)
pcs_spawned(f) :- pcs_spawn_arg(ct), pp_target_at(ct, f).
.decl pcs_called_otherwise(f: symbol)
pcs_called_otherwise(f) :- pcs_spawned(f), pp_target_at(ct, f), !pcs_spawn_arg(ct).

// Hand-offs. pcs_arg_of(a, cc): a is a positional or keyword argument of call cc, parentheses off.
.decl pcs_arg_of(a: node, cc: node)
pcs_arg_of(a, cc) :- kind(cc, "call"), pcs_call_value(cc, a).
// pcs_consumer(cc): a coroutine handed to the call whose term is cc is awaited for the caller: cc is awaited or
// iterated with `async for`, is an asyncio function other than a spawn or a runner (pcs_consumer_here), or calls a
// def of the run that awaits one of its parameters (pcs_awaits_param, stated in its file).
.decl pcs_consumer(cct: symbol)
pcs_consumer(cct) :- pcs_consumer_here(cc), pt_tm(cc, cct).
pcs_consumer(cct) :- pp_target_at(cct, g), pcs_awaits_param(g).
.decl pcs_consumer_here(cc: node)
pcs_consumer_here(cc) :- kind(cc, "call"), child(w, cc0, 0), kind(w, "await"), unparen(cc0, cc).
pcs_consumer_here(cc) :- kind(l, "for_statement"), op(l, "async"), field(l, "right", r), unparen(r, cc),
    kind(cc, "call").
pcs_consumer_here(cc) :- exc_call(cc, q), prefix("asyncio.", q), !pp_spawn_call(cc, _), !pcs_coro_runner(cc).
.decl pcs_awaits_param(g: symbol)
pcs_awaits_param(gq) :- kind(w, "await"), child(w, e0, 0), unparen(e0, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, p),
    pp_frame(w, g), param_named(g, p, _), pt_def(g, gq).
// pcs_handoff(c): the call whose term is c is handed, unawaited, to a call that does not await it for the caller.
.decl pcs_handoff(ct: symbol)
pcs_handoff(ct) :- pcs_arg_call(ct, cct), !pcs_consumer(cct).
.decl pcs_arg_call(ct: symbol, cct: symbol)
pcs_arg_call(ct, cct) :- pcs_arg_of(c, cc), kind(c, "call"), pt_tm(c, ct), pt_tm(cc, cct).
// pcs_handed_off(f): f runs for someone other than an awaiting caller of the run: one of its calls is handed off,
// it is passed uncalled to such a call, or a decorator called on an object registers it (`@router.websocket("/ws")`).
.decl pcs_handed_off(f: symbol)
pcs_handed_off(f) :- pcs_handoff(ct), pp_target_at(ct, f).
pcs_handed_off(f) :- pcs_arg_ref(cct, k, x), !pcs_consumer(cct), pcs_ref_def(k, x, f).
pcs_handed_off(fq) :- pp_async_def(f), dexpr(f, e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), kind(fn, "attribute"),
    !sym_of(fn, _), !call_target(e, _), pt_def(f, fq).
// pcs_arg_ref(cc, k, x): an argument of the call whose term is cc (not functools.partial) names a def (pcs_ref).
.decl pcs_arg_ref(cct: symbol, k: symbol, x: symbol)
pcs_arg_ref(cct, k, x) :- pcs_arg_of(e, cc), pcs_ref(e, k, x), !exc_call(cc, "functools.partial"), pt_tm(cc, cct).
// pcs_ref(e, k, x): e names a def without calling it: through imports (k "", x the name it resolves to), `self.m` in
// a method of class k (x = m), or `functools.partial(<one of those>, ...)`. pcs_ref_def(k, x, f): such a reference
// names async def f: the def of that qualified name, or what class k resolves m to.
.decl pcs_ref(e: node, k: symbol, x: symbol)
pcs_ref(e, "", q) :- pp_fn_ref(e, q).
pcs_ref(e, cq, m) :- attr_of(e, o, m), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, "self"), !field(_, "function", e),
    pp_frame(e, h), pp_frame(h, c), kind(c, "class_definition"), class_def(c, cq).
pcs_ref(e, k, x) :- exc_call(e, "functools.partial"), exc_arg(e, 0, r), pcs_ref(r, k, x).
.decl pcs_ref_used(k: symbol, x: symbol)
pcs_ref_used(k, x) :- pcs_runner_ref(k, x).
pcs_ref_used(k, x) :- pcs_arg_ref(_, k, x).
.decl pcs_ref_def(k: symbol, x: symbol, f: symbol)
pcs_ref_def("", q, f) :- pcs_ref_used("", q), pp_def_q(q, f), pp_async_sym(f).
pcs_ref_def(cq, m, f) :- pcs_ref_used(cq, m), cq != "", mro_method_sym(cq, m, f), pp_async_sym(f).
// pcs_consumed(f): a call of f outside test code is awaited by its caller (anything but a spawn or a hand-off).
.decl pcs_consumed(f: symbol)
pcs_consumed(f) :- pcs_handed_off(f), pp_target_at(ct, f), pcs_live_call(ct), !pcs_spawn_arg(ct), !pcs_handoff(ct).
.decl pcs_live_call(ct: symbol)
pcs_live_call(ct) :- kind(c, "call"), pp_live(c), pt_tm(c, ct).

// pcs_deferred(x, f): handler x sets a flag `v = True`, and later in f's own frame an `if` that tests v raises
// CancelledError (a bare `raise` there would raise nothing caught, so only a raise of the class counts).
.decl pcs_deferred(x: node, f: node)
pcs_deferred(x, f) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), exc_body(x, b), kind(a, "assignment"), within(a, b), pp_frame(a, f),
    field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, v), field(a, "right", r), kind(r, "true"),
    kind(i, "if_statement"), pp_frame(i, f), earlier(x, i), field(i, "condition", k0), unparen(k0, k),
    kind(k, "identifier"), text(k, v), field(i, "consequence", c), kind(rs, "raise_statement"), within(rs, c),
    exc_raise(rs, e), exc_class(e, cl), exc_qual(cl, q), pcs_cancel_q(q).

// pcs_inside_ok(n): the handler or suppress whose term is n sits in the body of a cancellation handler y of the same
// function that re-raises on every path (pcs_inside_at, stated in their file; pcs_reraised).
.decl pcs_inside_ok(nt: symbol)
pcs_inside_ok(nt) :- pcs_inside_at(nt, yt), pcs_reraised(yt).
.decl pcs_inside_at(nt: symbol, yt: symbol)
pcs_inside_at(nt, yt) :- pcs_handler(n, _, f), pcs_handler(y, _, f), y != n, exc_body(y, yb), within(n, yb),
    pt_tm(n, nt), pt_tm(y, yt).
pcs_inside_at(nt, yt) :- pcs_suppress(n, f), pcs_handler(y, _, f), exc_body(y, yb), within(n, yb), pt_tm(n, nt),
    pt_tm(y, yt).

// ---- anyio and trio ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// pcs_anyio_handler(x, f) / pcs_anyio_suppress(w, f): x (w) catches cancellation only as BaseException or bare, in
// a function whose own frame uses anyio or trio.
.decl pcs_anyio_handler(x: node, f: node)
pcs_anyio_handler(x, f) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), !pcs_names_asyncio(x), pcs_anyio(f).
.decl pcs_anyio_suppress(w: node, f: node)
pcs_anyio_suppress(w, f) :- pcs_suppress(w, f), !pcs_suppress_names_asyncio(w), pcs_anyio(f).
.decl pcs_broad_fn(f: node)
pcs_broad_fn(f) :- pcs_handler(x, _, f), !pcs_names_asyncio(x).
pcs_broad_fn(f) :- pcs_suppress(w, f), !pcs_suppress_names_asyncio(w).
// pcs_anyio(f): a name in f's own frame resolves into anyio or trio.
.decl pcs_anyio(f: node)
pcs_anyio(f) :- pcs_broad_fn(f), kind(n, "identifier"), within(n, f), pp_frame(n, f), sym_of(n, q),
    (q = "anyio" ; q = "trio" ; prefix("anyio.", q) ; prefix("trio.", q)).

